in other news a jury in chicago has  found jesse smallett guilty of staging a  racist anti-gay attack on himself and  then lying to police about it the former  empire actor was convicted on five of  the six charges connected to this highly  publicized incident he now faces up to  three years in prison charlie demar has  been covering the trial for us  jessie smallett said nothing moments  after jurors found him guilty on five of  the six counts of disorderly conduct  after deliberating for just over nine  hours he was found not guilty on count  six which involved a later report to  police they found mr smallett guilty of  virtually all charges of doing exactly  what we said he did  the five counts stem from smilet telling  police in january 2019 that he'd been  attacked by two men  beat him up doused him in bleach and put  a rope around his neck initially  identified by smilet as his attackers  brothers abel and ola osindaro both  testified last week that smullett  orchestrated the hoax and paid them 3  500 dollars to stage the attack smolette  himself took the stand maintaining his  innocence and that there was no hoax mr  smallett would not have lost this case  as he did today unless the jury found  that he lied to them but smilet was  found not guilty on count six reporting  in february the following month to a  detective that he'd been the victim of  an aggravated battery you cannot say  jesse is lying and just is not lying for  the same exact  incident so we feel 100 percent  confident  that this case will be  won on appeal attorney joe tamborino  says the jury might have felt they had  already convicted smilet on enough  counts they could have decided that  perhaps the sixth count maybe they found  that with that one particular officer  there really wasn't a lie  smellette says the actor is smut's  attorney rather says the actor is  committed to clearing his name the judge  set a post-trial hearing for the end of  january and  the sentencing date has yet to be set  nate  charlie thank you
 

